.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:383:## 6. Scenario fixtures
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:385:### NP-GT-001 — ordinary critique/revise/finalize success
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:387:**Inputs:** ordinary brief; critique lens set `{correctness, scope}`; gate outcomes `iterate`, then `proceed`; final review `approved`.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:396:megaplan/critique-cycle/0/gate[iterate]
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:400:megaplan/critique-cycle/1/gate[proceed]
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:409:**Typed decisions:** gate generation 0 accepts/consumes `iterate`; gate generation 1 accepts/consumes `proceed`; review accepts/consumes `approved`; terminal accepts/consumes `done`. Each has a different Run Authority decision ID and the exact matching CAS sequence.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:415:**Checkpoint/reentry:** checkpoint after revise and before the second critique generation; no reentry.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:419:**Forbidden:** direct gate-to-finalize after `iterate`; a second revise; handler/status-selected next step; a delivery cycle copied under a second entry route; shared semantic/RA/WBC/custody ID.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:421:**Mutations:** changing the authored first gate branch to `proceed` changes the trace and fixture fails; changing a legacy route map or handler `next_step` does not; deleting one same-named critique child is detected as a multiplicity failure.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:427:### NP-GT-002 — dynamic critique retry and sequential fallback
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:429:**Inputs:** dynamic lenses `{correctness, security, api}`; `security` fails transiently once; the declared parallel launcher becomes unavailable before any child effect; policy permits sequential fallback; gate proceeds.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:439:.../gate[proceed]
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:449:aggregate terminal of the semantic `security` child. An accepted retry decision
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:450:opens attempt/retry generation 1. Success accepts the child's one aggregate
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:460:**Checkpoint/reentry:** retry checkpoint records cap consumption and all digests; no host reentry.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:470:durable model/tool result but before checkpoint reuses that result and retains
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:475:### NP-GT-003 — human clarification suspension and cross-host resume
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:502:**Checkpoint/reentry:** checkpoint contains the prep semantic cursor, human input schema, authority subject/fence, WBC attempt lineage, custody target/epoch, and the program/policy/WBC/installed digests. Host B verifies exact equality before product code. A mismatch yields admitted quarantine/migration handling, not implicit continuation.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:506:**Forbidden:** marker-only resume; reuse of Host A epoch; resume selected from status/projection; plan body before exact digest/authority/custody checks; silent migration; duplicate human decision consumption.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:509:Replacing production-store CAS with application read/check/write, a process
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:523:### NP-GT-004 — external effect outcome before receipt, then crash
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:525:**Inputs:** delivery tasks `T1`, `T2`, `T3` in batch `B1`; external effect `E-T2`; crash occurs after the external system returns success and durable `wbc.effect.outcome`, before the product receipt/projection is written.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:542:**WBC/effects:** exactly one `E-T2` intent that reaches the external system and exactly one terminal success outcome. Missing product receipt is rebuilt as a projection from the durable outcome. If only intent were durable, the run would enter WBC ambiguity/reconciliation rather than guessing.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:544:**Checkpoint/reentry:** checkpoint after T1 and at T2 effect outcome; new host/worker verifies digests and current authority/custody before reconciliation.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:548:**Forbidden:** repeating `E-T2`; treating absence of a product receipt as evidence the effect did not happen; an index path; two writers during compatibility cutover; completing from a forged receipt.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:550:**Mutations:** crash injection before intent, after intent, after outcome, and after receipt must yield the admitted four distinct histories; deleting the outcome causes ambiguity rather than replay-as-success; changing an old execute handler is inert after cutover.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:559:### NP-GT-005 — review failure, bounded scoped rework, refinalization
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:578:**Decisions:** exact review aggregate decision `rework`; scoped rework/refinalization decision names `{T2}`; second review `approved`; terminal `done`. Cap state is source/policy visible and durable.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:585:`superseded_by_named_exit` control terminal for every intervening durable scope
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:600:with identical task IDs. State/checkpoint/artifact/effect/cache namespaces must
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:605:### NP-GT-006 — config override, note effect, publication/cancellation race
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:609:**Shared prefix:** an admitted `set-model` request is translated to a typed authority decision and typed reconfigure transition carrying a schema-versioned delta. It durably checkpoints, binds the changed policy/executable/product-contract identity, advances reentry identity as required, and resumes the exact semantic cursor. Ambient context/live flags remain inert. An `add-note` request produces a WBC effect targeted at the exact semantic occurrence and an explicit `no_route_change` outcome. Neither CLI request directly dispatches product work.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:620:records `decision.invalidated` and requires a new request. A consumed decision
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:650:### NP-DX-001 through NP-DX-004 — authoring execution modes
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:671:  no durable checkpoint/replay/resume/admission/certification receipt exists;
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:676:authority class are independent, explicit proof fields.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:678:## 7. Mandatory mutation suite
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:691:| Reorder dynamic input list | Same semantic child identities and aggregate result |
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:692:| Forge or stale a projection/receipt/status field | No dispatch, route, completion, resume, cancel, publish, or delivery change |
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:693:| Switch checkout/wheel/cloud implementation | Same normalized trace |
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:696:| Append comparison WBC/checkpoint/effect/terminal history | Excluded/rejected; never resumable, authoritative, or promotable |
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:702:| Treat a retryable attempt terminal as the aggregate child terminal, or contribute twice to the reducer | Child-terminal cardinality/consumption fails |
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:705:| Redispatch a semantically invalidated or consumed decision | Rejected; actor-local still-valid unconsumed redispatch remains the only allowed case |
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:710:| Restore a Native durable record outside its declared rollback boundary | Restore-then-replay proof fails |
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:712:| Replace canonical CAS with application read/check/write, local locking, serialized clients or in-memory atomicity | Two-client production-adapter contention/crash proof fails |
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:713:| Forge, omit or relabel a comparison token/provenance field, or register it as admitted | Shared validator/query/proof exclusion fails; history is never promoted |
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:715:| Change the field table/allowlist without an accepted amendment receipt and replaying every affected dependent receipt | Old evidence is invalid for the new table version; comparison/certification fails |
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:716:| Roll back/truncate a proof registry or replay a receipt under another store incarnation/high-water cursor | Receipt validation and restore-then-replay proof fail |
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:718:| Change one gate vocabulary site, precedence order or no-progress flag identity set without a total migration mapping | Compile/exhaustiveness fails or emits bounded `progress_incomparable`; the ordinary streak is never silently reset/carried |
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:719:| Use the whole payload, an open string or an undeclared field as a route discriminant | Static route-key validation fails |
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:723:| Reuse a source-run authority, effect idempotency key, cache namespace or checkpoint namespace in a fork | Always-hard isolation assertion fails |
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:725:| Emit a durable checkpoint or replay/certification receipt from unsupported preview | Preview-disposition assertion fails |
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:728:## 8. Twelve-milestone adoption
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:730:- **S1:** check in the schema, independent source-oracle/raw-export/verifier contract, six scenario and four `NP-DX` skeletons, forbidden-source vocabulary, multiplicity/order predicates, and mutation interface. Freeze the five-mode execution and enforcement-disposition matrix, certified-CAS provenance, registry/manifest evolution and receipt incarnation/high-water contracts. Prove the comparator on synthetic/raw mutations; current product behavior may remain red.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:737:  binding/evaluation schemas, evidence scope/proof modes, aggregation
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:740:  projection-invariance proof without authority.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:741:- **S2R:** consume GO-FORMAT and C1/C2; integrate the independent proof path with the neutral production runtime; fill generic loop, fanout/fanin, decision, policy, identity, checkpoint and retry/fallback events; instantiate concrete child-set/aggregation semantics for every primitive; implement edit/repeat/fork with isolated identities; register all three planes, pass production-adapter two-client CAS/crash and introduction-time restore proofs, and close GO-0 through the sole kernel-enablement transition.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:742:- **S3A:** make prep/plan/critique through the join green, land execution-plane resume binding and the typed gate seam, and close GO-1A.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:743:- **S3B:** freeze the eight-value gate vocabulary, precedence and canonical no-progress predicate; make gate/revise and `NP-GT-001/002` green, remove the S3A seam, own the typed tiebreaker/finalize seam and close GO-1B/GO-1.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:745:- **S5A:** make the full finalize/admit/execute/evidence/accept/review/reopen-or-new-work/aggregate topology green in comparison/shadow execution, reject false done and executable `REVIEW`, inventory every effect-protocol class, and close per-class GO-2 without live effect authority.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:746:- **S5B:** require the accepted GO-2 and exact Custody bounded-projection receipts at the live authority switch, then make `NP-GT-004` and `NP-GT-005` green against the admitted live-effect and bounded review/rework paths, including the 57k no-full-history-fallback gate.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:748:- **S7:** run every fixture and mutation against checkout, built wheel, and cloud; compare ordered/multiset normalized traces from one run history, not separately manufactured row evidence.
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:751:  receipt incarnation/high-water binding, comparison-token/volatile-field
.megaplan/initiatives/megaplan-native-parity-corrective/GOLDEN_TRACE_CONTRACT.md:755:## 9. What this contract deliberately does not specify
