Inventory is complete. Preservation map, in condensed form:

- Completion M1 → Native C1 (neutral spec/identity/shadow); M2 → C2 signatures/evaluator in shadow plus S2R concrete instances and first enforcement; M3 → S5A shadow/S5B live slice; M4 → C1/C2/S2R plus Native S3A–S7 adoption; M5 → Platform S1–S6.
- Native S1, S2F, C1, C2, S2R, S3A, S3B, S4, S5A, S5B, S6, S7 and every named receipt/golden fixture are retained. Old `m*`/combined briefs remain historical appendices, not launch contracts.
- Platform S1–S6 all remain: inventory → neutral extraction → authoring core → DX → isolated recomposition → adversarial consumer → certification.
- M11/Custody manifests, bounded-projection/57k receipts, false-pass traces, restore evidence, and all evidence consumed by existing manifests are protected from supersession.
- The two actionable defects are: narrative gates are missing from both executable chain manifests, and several oracle amendments are still prose-only. I’m now fixing both, while keeping the Completion source initiative non-launchable and byte-preserving its historical briefs/proposal.
