---
name: context-usage
description: >
  Report how full the context window is and how it grew over a session, by
  reading the on-disk session transcript. Plots turn-by-turn token growth and
  marks every compaction boundary (auto or manual) for Claude Code, Codex, and
  Hermes. Use when the user asks how many tokens are in context, how context
  grew, when compaction happened, or wants a token-growth chart the built-in
  /context can't produce.
allowed-tools: Bash(*context_usage*), Bash(*context-usage*), Bash(jq *), Bash(find *)
---

# Context Usage

## What It Does

Reconstructs context-window usage from the JSONL transcripts Claude Code, Codex,
and Hermes write to disk. Unlike the built-in `/context` (live, exact,
per-category, but single-point-in-time), this gives the **trajectory**: how big
the context was at each assistant turn across the whole session, plus where
compaction reset it.

## How To Run

```bash
~/.claude/skills/context-usage/context_usage.sh                 # current Claude project (latest session)
~/.claude/skills/context-usage/context_usage.sh --codex         # latest Codex session
~/.claude/skills/context-usage/context_usage.sh --hermes        # latest Hermes transcript
~/.claude/skills/context-usage/context_usage.sh --session /path/to/x.jsonl
~/.claude/skills/context-usage/context_usage.sh --cwd /path/to/repo
~/.claude/skills/context-usage/context_usage.sh --json          # raw events
```

## How It Works

- **Claude**: `~/.claude/projects/<cwd-with-slashes-as-dashes>/*.jsonl`. Each
  `type:"assistant"` line carries `message.usage`. Context size at that turn =
  `input_tokens + cache_creation_input_tokens + cache_read_input_tokens`.
- **Codex**: `~/.codex/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/*.jsonl`. `token_count` events carry
  `last_token_usage` and `model_context_window`.
- **Hermes**: runs *on* Claude Code, so its transcripts are Claude-format but
  nested under `~/.claude/projects/-Users-peteromalley-Documents-hermes-agent/<session>/subagents/*.jsonl`.
  `--hermes` finds the latest and parses it with the Claude path.

### Compaction detection (explicit in both)

- **Claude**: a `type:"system"`, `subtype:"compact_boundary"` line with
  `compactMetadata.{trigger, preTokens, postTokens, durationMs}`. The companion
  summary message is flagged `isCompactSummary:true`. Detection is unambiguous.
- **Codex**: an `event_msg` with `payload.type:"context_compacted"` (plus
  `compaction`/`compacted` response items carrying `replacement_history`).

## Caveats

- The transcript lags the live window by one turn (the in-flight turn isn't
  written yet) and has no per-category breakdown — for the live snapshot use
  `/context`.
- The default Claude window is assumed 1M (Opus 4.7) when the transcript
  doesn't state one; Codex reports its own `model_context_window`.

